// Saga ([CR#714]) — the enchantment subtype whose registry row confers the
// rules OF THE SUBTYPE (as `Innate` / registry properties, never card
// text):
//
//   - ENTERS with a lore counter ([CR#714.3a] — "This Saga enters with a
//     lore counter on it", a [CR#614.1c] self-replacement): the same
//     `Also(would: ThisEnters, …)` augment Modular uses. Read-ahead sagas
//     ([CR#714.3b]) choose their starting chapter instead — a future row.
//   - The TURN-BASED lore increment ([CR#714.3c] — as a player's precombat
//     main phase begins, that player puts a lore counter on each Saga they
//     control; no stack): `TurnBased` fires on the BEARER'S CONTROLLER'S
//     own precombat main. Engine execution of registry `TurnBased` rows is
//     stage 3; the chapter triggers themselves execute today.
//
// The FINAL-CHAPTER sacrifice SBA ([CR#714.4]) needs the card's own final
// chapter number ([CR#714.2d] — the greatest threshold among ITS chapter
// abilities), which a generic registry row cannot name; it is spelled
// card-side as `Sba(when: Compare(CounterCount(This, LoreCounter),
// AtLeast, <final>), then: Sacrifice(This))` — the Idris History of
// Benalia exemplar. Chapters themselves are the `Chapter` ability macro
// ([CR#714.2b]).
(
    name: "Saga",
    kinds: [Subtype],
    body: Subtype(
        name: "Saga",
        types: [Enchantment],
        confers: [
            // [CR#714.3a]: enters with a lore counter.
            Ability(Innate(Static(effects: [
                Replacement(Also(
                    would: ThisEnters,
                    also: PutCounters(This, LoreCounter, 1),
                )),
            ]))),
            // [CR#714.3c]: the turn-based lore increment.
            TurnBased(
                at: PrecombatMain,
                effect: PutCounters(This, LoreCounter, 1),
            ),
        ],
    ),
)
